    "comments": [
      {
        "url": "https://github.com/google/osv-scanner/issues/3093#issuecomment-5950073574",
        "author": "Denimworld12",
        "body": "Confirmed on `main` (`1b86129`), and it is already captured in this repo's own snapshots.\n\n`mapIDsToGroupedSARIFFinding` points every ID in an alias group at the same `*groupedSARIFFinding` (`internal/output/result.go:229-231`), and `PrintSARIFReport` iterates every key of that map (`internal/output/sarif.go:266`), so one group emits one result per matched ID.\n\n`sarif_test.snap`, \"one source with one package and two aliases of a single vulnerability\":\n\n```\nruleId=OSV-1  location=path/to/my/first/lockfile  fingerprint=[line-hash]\nruleId=OSV-1  location=path/to/my/first/lockfile  fingerprint=[line-hash]\n```\n\nIdentical in `ruleId`, `locations`, `message.text` and `partialFingerprints`. Fourteen snapshot cases currently contain a duplicated `ruleId`.\n\nWorth separating from the legitimate case, since the fix has to keep it. \"two sources with the same vulnerable package\":\n\n```\nruleId=OSV-1  location=path/to/my/first/lockfile\nruleId=OSV-1  location=path/to/my/second/lockfile\n```\n\nSame rule, different locations, two real findings. So the discriminator is the location, not the rule: alias duplicates collapse, per-source results stay. That means one result per group rather than per ID, with the `pkgSourceSet` loop at `sarif.go:340` continuing to produce one result per source.\n\n@pmig you mentioned drafting a PR — are you still on it? If so I'll leave it with you. If not, could this be assigned to me? The change is small and everything downstream already keys off `gv.DisplayID`; the bulk of the diff would be the snapshot regen via `make test SNAPS=true`.\n"
      },
      {
        "url": "https://github.com/google/osv-scanner/issues/3093#issuecomment-5990197277",
        "author": "pmig",
        "body": "@Denimworld12 let's wait for a mantainers response, if they want to implement deduplication. @Ly-Joey or @G-Rath is this something you would be open to accept contributions or is this an expected behavior?"
      }
    ],
